 "data_limits": [
  "Slices are alternatives, not additive: each is solved alone against the shared BU RWA and EL budgets.",
  "New lending is assumed Stage 1 at the slice's current EL rate and CRWA risk weight; pricing, tenor, region, collateral type and structure (Islamic share) of the new business are not known in advance and are not constrained here.",
  "RAROC now is the Book drift engine's one-year RAROC on the existing facilities of the slice; it is a guide to the hurdle a new deal would clear at today's pricing, not a quote.",
  "Group headroom uses the relationship domain's connected groups (two or more members) and Tier 1 from the capital parameter table; an approved group cap tighter than the policy limit (Deal Desk group exposure) is not applied here."
 ],
 "method": [
  "Each risk-appetite metric is recomputed with the slice's new lending added; the largest X keeping it at or under its appetite level is found by bisection; the slice headroom is the smallest X and its constraint is binding.",
  "A metric already beyond its level allows only lending that does not worsen it.",
  "Hurdle: returns.hurdle (sector override) vs EAD-weighted median RAROC now; margin uplift = (hurdle - RAROC) / dRAROC/dmargin."
 ],
